    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "",
    "lawSection": "Real Property Taxation",
    "memo": "BILL NUMBER:S5006\n\nTITLE OF BILL:  An act to authorize St. Peter and Paul Ukrainian\nCatholic Church to apply for exemption from real property taxes\npursuant to section 420-a of the real property tax law\n\nPURPOSE:\n\nTo authorize St. Peter and Paul Ukrainian Catholic Church to apply for\nexemption from real property taxes pursuant to section 420-a of the\nreal property tax law.\n\nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 allows the assessor of the Town of Ramapo, of Rockland\nCounty, to accept and review an application from the St. Peter and\nPaul Ukrainian Catholic Church for a nonprofit real property tax\nexemption for the 2010 assessment roll, as if it had been received on\nor before the applicable taxable status date.\n\nIn addition, Section 1 allows the assessor of the Village of Spring\nValley, of Rockland County, to accept and review an application from\nthe St. Peter and Paul Ukrainian Catholic Church for a nonprofit real\nproperty tax exemption for the 2011 assessment toll, as if it had been\nreceived on or before the applicable taxable status date.\n\nSection 2 provides for an immediate effective date.\n\nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThe St. Peter and Paul Ukrainian Catholic Church is a nonprofit\norganization that would be otherwise entitled to an exemption under\nSection 420-a of the Real Property Tax Law had the organization filed\nan application for the exemption by the appropriate taxable status\ndate.\n\nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill.\n\nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone to state.\n\nEFFECTIVE DATE:\n\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n\n",
